  "root_problem": "Billing dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from ~600-610/month (Jun-Jul) to ~1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-07), driven in material part by a drop in manual meter-read route completion to 0.88 against a 0.95 target during a field-reader staffing shortfall since July (E-03, E-06), which pushed billing's estimate-substitution step to issue more ESTIMATED-read bills (41% of disputed bills carry read_type ESTIMATED, E-02). This is distinct from the requester's framing: ticket response time is within SLA (E-04) and no tariff change occurred (E-01, E-05), so slow ticket handling and a legitimate rate increase are ruled out as causes."
